cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Modelstamp in your research, please cite the software and the preferred preprint below."
title: "Modelstamp: Integrity and environment verification for Python machine-learning artifacts"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dhekne
    given-names: Anagha
repository-code: "https://github.com/AnaghaDhekne/modelstamp"
url: "https://anaghadhekne.github.io/modelstamp/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.4
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22047771
date-released: 2026-08-25
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - model persistence
  - reproducibility
  - artifact integrity
  - dependency drift
  - model provenance
  - scikit-learn
abstract: >-
  Modelstamp is a Python package that records integrity, environment, and model
  metadata alongside serialized machine-learning artifacts. It verifies an
  artifact before deserialization and reports relevant dependency differences
  between the saved and current environments. Optional HMAC authentication can
  be used when publishers and verifiers share a protected secret.
